1
00:00:00,050 --> 00:00:09,596
Nucleotides join through phosphodiester bonds, linking carbon three of one sugar to carbon five of the next through a phosphate.

2
00:00:09,596 --> 00:00:17,630
So a strand has a free phosphate at one end, the five prime end, and a free hydroxyl at the other, the three prime end.

3
00:00:17,630 --> 00:00:19,609
A strand has a direction.

